'''Firstlight Noya''' or '''Alina''' is a Trekker.

Her original version is [[Noya]].

== Profile ==
''"Swinging a greatsword that buried her past, Noya relies on years of brutal arena combat to carve out a path to the future."''

== Stats ==

==Skills==
{{TrekkerSkill
| name = Honed Sword Art
| brief = Wields the greatsword and longsword to deal continuous attacks. When farther away from the target, Firstlight Noya performs a sprint attack with the longsword. Increases the DMG multiplier dealt by Firstlight Noya's Auto Attacks against targets with {{word|Glimmer|}}.<br>Upgrade materials: {{Item|Radiant Feather Crown}} {{Item|Chess Piece of Skill}} {{Item|Kung Fu Game Cartridge}} {{Item|Fighting Game Cartridge}} {{Item|Phantom Game Cartridge}}
| desc_1 = Wields the greatsword [Daybreak] and the longsword [Dawn] to deal continuous attacks. Strike 1: Swings the greatsword, dealing {{color|#fb8037|45% x2}} of Max HP as Lux Auto Attack DMG. Strike 2: Swings the greatsword, dealing {{color|#fb8037|46% x3}} of Max HP as Lux Auto Attack DMG. Strike 3: Swings the greatsword, dealing {{color|#fb8037|66% x2}} of Max HP as Lux Auto Attack DMG. Strike 4: Swings the longsword and fires 2 Glows, each dealing {{color|#fb8037|21%}} of Max HP as Lux Skill DMG. When Firstlight Noya is farther away from the target, her Auto Attacks become a sprint attack with the longsword, dealing {{color|#fb8037|30% x3}} of Max HP as Lux Skill DMG. This effect can be triggered once every 1.5s. When Firstlight Noya's Auto Attacks deal DMG to a target with {{word|Glimmer|}}, each stack of {{word|Glimmer|}} on the target increases the DMG multiplier of this attack by {{color|#fb8037|4.2%}}.<br>Upgrade materials: {{Item|Kung Fu Game Cartridge|quantity=6}} {{Item|Chess Piece of Skill|quantity=2}} {{Item|Dorra|quantity=13300}}
| desc_2 = Wields the greatsword [Daybreak] and the longsword [Dawn] to deal continuous attacks. Strike 1: Swings the greatsword, dealing {{color|#fb8037|51% x2}} of Max HP as Lux Auto Attack DMG. Strike 2: Swings the greatsword, dealing {{color|#fb8037|53% x3}} of Max HP as Lux Auto Attack DMG. Strike 3: Swings the greatsword, dealing {{color|#fb8037|76% x2}} of Max HP as Lux Auto Attack DMG. Strike 4: Swings the longsword and fires 2 Glows, each dealing {{color|#fb8037|25%}} of Max HP as Lux Skill DMG. When Firstlight Noya is farther away from the target, her Auto Attacks become a sprint attack with the longsword, dealing {{color|#fb8037|35% x3}} of Max HP as Lux Skill DMG. This effect can be triggered once every 1.5s. When Firstlight Noya's Auto Attacks deal DMG to a target with {{word|Glimmer|}}, each stack of {{word|Glimmer|}} on the target increases the DMG multiplier of this attack by {{color|#fb8037|4.9%}}.<br>Upgrade materials: {{Item|Kung Fu Game Cartridge|quantity=12}} {{Item|Chess Piece of Skill|quantity=6}} {{Item|Dorra|quantity=17600}}
